    "content" : "Proof of Claim 10. Notice that for every 3 ≤ p ≤ 100 s − 1, there is a path of length p contained in the copy of H ( s ) in G connecting v i and v i +1 , where i ∈ [ s ℓ ] and v i ,v i +1 ∈ V ( G 1 ). Moreover, every edge in E 3 lies in a path of length 100 s − 1 contained in the copy of H ( s ) in G connecting v j and v j +1 for some j ∈ [ s ℓ ], where v j ,v j +1 ∈ V ( G 1 ). Thus using the Hamilton cycle in G 1 , we can find a cycle of each length k , k ≥ 3 s ℓ + 100 s containing e for every e ∈ E 3 ."
